<article class="env-lemma" id="015N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/015N">Lemma <span data-tag="015N">13.22.2</span> <span class="named">(Grothendieck spectral sequence)</span>.</a>  With assumptions as in Lemma <a href="/tag/015M" data-tag="015M">13.22.1</a> and assuming the equivalent conditions (1) and (2) hold. Let $X$ be an object of $D^{+}(\mathcal{A})$. There exists a spectral sequence $(E_ r, d_ r)_{r \geq 0}$ consisting of bigraded objects $E_ r$ of $\mathcal{C}$ with $d_ r$ of bidegree $(r, - r + 1)$ and with </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E_2^{p, q} = R^ pG(H^ q(RF(X)))  \]
</div>
  <p> Moreover, this spectral sequence is bounded, converges to $H^*(R(G \circ F)(X))$, and induces a finite filtration on each $H^ n(R(G \circ F)(X))$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We may represent $X$ by a bounded below complex $A^\bullet $. Choose an injective resolution $A^\bullet \to I^\bullet $. Choose a Cartan-Eilenberg resolution $F(I^\bullet ) \to I^{\bullet , \bullet }$ using Lemma <a href="/tag/015I" data-tag="015I">13.21.2</a>. Apply the second spectral sequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/015J" data-tag="015J">13.21.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>